The '''Quarren''', also known by the derogatory nickname "'''Squid Heads'''," were a [[humanoid]], [[squid]]-like [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Mon Cala]], where they coexisted with the [[Mon Calamari]] in a peaceful, albeit tense, relationship.

==Biology and appearance==
The Quarren were a bipedal [[squid]]-like [[species]] with four facial tentacles which protruded from their lower jaw. Their skin-[[color]] range included various hues of orange,<ref name="USW" /> salmon,<ref name="Pursuit of Peace" /> tan,<ref name="DB Quarren" /> pink,<ref name="Darth Maul 2" /> and purple.<ref name="Star Wars Annual 1" /> They had a pair of deep turquoise [[eye]]s, finned [[Limb|hands]] with suction-tipped fingers,<ref name="DB Quarren" /> and small<ref name="Water War" /> tusks<ref name="Convergence">''[[The High Republic: Convergence]]''</ref> on their mouth.<ref name="Water War" /> In the two long protrusions that extended from either side of their faces, Quarren had gill-like structures that were actually hearing organs.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> While the [[Quarrenese]] was the native [[language]] of the Quarren,<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref> the species was also able to speak fluent<ref name="Pursuit of Peace" /> [[Galactic Basic Standard]].<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" />

[[File:CalgrizMaul-2017DarthMaul2.png|thumb|left|200px|The Quarren Calgriz spits ink at Darth Maul in combat.]]
[[Homeworld|Native]] to the<ref name="DB Quarren" /> [[Water|aquatic]]<ref name="Water War" /> world of [[Mon Cala]], the Quarren were natural swimmers<ref name="DB Quarren" /> and were most comfortable underwater, prefering to be immersed in liquid.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> They were also bipedal beings that could walk<ref name="Pursuit of Peace" /> and sit upright.<ref name="DB Quarren" /> Capable of spitting clouds of black ink as a defensive measure in combat,<ref name="Darth Maul 2" /> such ink could also be released from a Quarren's body when cut open at the mid-section by a [[lightsaber]], a [[Death|mortal]] act.<ref name="Kylo Ren 3">[[The Rise of Kylo Ren 3|''The Rise of Kylo Ren'' 3]]</ref> Quarrens would also release ink in their [[sleep]] during [[Dream|nightmares]]. Any atmosphere without humidity could be bad for a Quarren's skin and nasal passages, resulting in off-world Quarren turning to products like [[moruga nut oil]] and taking extremely hot showers.<ref name="Convergence" />

Similar to their neighboring [[Sentience|sentient]] species&mdash;the [[Mon Calamari]]&mdash;who shared their homeworld, the Quarren typically wore [[clothing]] that covered most of their body, though left their heads unadorned.<ref name="Water War" /><ref name="Episode I">{{Film|I}}</ref><ref name="Choose Your Destiny">''[[Choose Your Destiny: A Han & Chewie Adventure]]''</ref> However, the Quarren [[pirate]] [[Kragan Gorr]] wore an [[Imperial officer battle armor]] [[helmet]].<ref name="The Triple Dark">{{Resistance|The Triple Dark}}</ref><ref name="Zero Hour TG">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/zero-hour-trivia-gallery|text="Zero Hour" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|Slide 9}}</ref>

The Quarren and Mon Calamari also shared the capability of sustaining [[Cybernetics|cybernetic modifications]].<ref name="Lightsaber Lost">{{TCW|Lightsaber Lost}}</ref><ref name="Vader 6">[[Darth Vader (2015) 6|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 6]]</ref> Additionally, a [[hybrid]] between the two [[Reproduction|existed]]<ref name="A Recipe for Death">{{StoryCite|story=A Recipe for Death|book=Tales from a Galaxy Far, Far Away: Aliens: Volume I}}</ref> during or prior to [[Galactic standard calendar|146 BBY]].<ref name="Date">"[[A Recipe for Death]]" establishes that [[Strono Tuggs]] has served in [[Takodana Castle]] for more than twenty [[Standard year|years]], and ''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]'' establishes that Tuggs served in the castle for [[Standard century|centuries]] before the [[Battle of Takodana]]. As such, "A Recipe for Death" must have taken place at least 180 years before the battle. As ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' establishes the occurrance of the battle to have been in [[34 ABY]], it could be found that "A Recipe for Death" took place during or prior to 146 BBY.</ref>

==History==
===Shared homeworld===
[[File:Political_pressure.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Tensions existed bewteen the Quarren and the Mon Calamari.]]
The Quarren shared their homeworld of Mon Cala with the Mon Calamari,<ref name="DB Quarren" /> another influential amphibious species who also preferred building their [[City|cities]] underwater.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> However, tensions existed between both species that made coexistence a struggle at times.<ref name="Water War" /> Around [[392 BBY]]<ref name="392 Date">''[[The High Republic: Convergence]]'', the events of which are dated to [[382 BBY]] per ''[[Star Wars: The High Republic Character Encyclopedia]]'', establishes [[Orlen Mollo]]'s visit to [[Mon Cala]] to address a territorial issue occurred nearly a [[Standard decade|decade]] before hand, placing it around [[392 BBY]].</ref> during the [[High Republic Era]], the Quarren [[Orlen Mollo]] returned to his homeworld to help negotiate the end to a [[Territory dispute on Mon Cala|territorial dispute]].<ref name="Convergence" /> Later in the High Republic age, one of [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Lina Soh]]'s planned [[Great Works]] was to negotiate a treaty between the Quarren and Mon Calamari.<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref> The Quarren also resided in large numbers on the estuary moon of [[Trask]];<ref name="Chapter 11">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 11: The Heiress}}</ref> the moon had been colonized by Quarren and Mon Calamari who hoped to leave behind the politics of Mon Cala.<ref name="Mando Handbook">''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian Handbook]]''</ref>

Around the [[time]] of the [[Trade Federation]]'s [[Invasion of Naboo]], a Quarren [[Senator]]<ref name="Episode I" /> named [[Tikkes]] represented Mon Cala in the [[Galactic Republic]] [[Galactic Senate|Senate]].<ref name="USW" /> During the [[Separatist Crisis]], Tikkes defected to the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]],<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref> and was replaced in the Galactic Senate by the Quarren [[Loyalist]] [[Tundra Dowmeia]].<ref name="USW" /> On the whole, the Quarren species leaned towards the Confederacy during the Clone Wars,<ref name="219 POV">{{InsiderCite|219|A Certain Point of View}}</ref> but there were pro-Republic Quarren all the same.<ref name="USW" /><ref name="Pursuit of Peace" /> Quarren engineers worked in the pro-Confederate [[Free Dac Volunteers Engineering Corps]].<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> The [[Quarren Isolation League]] pushed for Quarren independence.<ref name="HC36">{{HelmetCollectionCite|36|Databank A-Z}}</ref>

===Battle of Mon Cala===
{{Quote|The Quarren are being used. I've seen it happen before. Count Dooku has deceived them.|Ahsoka Tano to Captain [[Gial Ackbar|Ackbar]], explaining the recent behavior of the Quarren|<ref name="Prisoners">{{TCW|Prisoners}}</ref>}}
Separatist Quarren were opposed in battle by the [[Mon Calamari Knights]].<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> During the [[Clone Wars]], the Separatists, acting through the [[Karkarodon]] [[advisor]] [[Riff Tamson]], stirred up trouble between the Quarren and the Mon Calamari. Following the [[assassin]]ation of the Mon Calamari [[King]] [[Yos Kolina]], the Quarren led by Chieftain [[Nossor Ri]] contested his son [[Prince]] [[Lee-Char]]'s claim to the throne. With the encouragement of Tamson, Ri called for new leadership and a chance for the Quarren to rule Mon Cala.<ref name="DB Nossor Ri">{{Databank|nossor-ri|Nossor Ri}}</ref> This led to a [[Battle of Mon Cala|civil war on Mon Cala]]: the Separatists backed the Quarren Isolation League,<ref name="USW" /> which made a play at conquering Mon Cala<ref name="HC36" /> with the Confederacy's military support, while the Republic supported the Mon Calamari. Prior to the outbreak of fighting, Senator [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] and her [[Jedi]] [[bodyguard]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] visited [[Coral City|Mon Cala city]] in attempt to broker peace between the two warring species.<ref name="Water War" />

However, the Quarren launched a preemptive strike on the [[City]] of Mon Cala with Separatist [[AQ-series battle droid]]s, but were repelled by the Mon Calamari's Jedi and [[Clone SCUBA trooper|clone allies]]. The Quarren then counter-attacked with [[Hydroid Medusa]]s, gigantic jellyfish with electrified tentacles, which succeeded in overwhelming the Mon Calamari and Republic allies. Soon after this, the Quarren were able to capture the [[Capital]]. The remaining Mon Calamari and Jedi forces were forced to retreat. Despite the victory, Ri was uneasy with his new Separatist allies after Tamson complied with [[Count]] [[Dooku]]'s orders to [[Slavery|enslave]] the Mon Calamari population.<ref name="Water War" />

[[File:LeeCharCrowned-Prisoners.jpg|thumb|300px|The Quarren celebrating Prince Lee Char's crowning.]]
Quarren forces then participated in a manhunt for several enemy fugitives including Prince Lee-Char, Senator Amidala, Skywalker, and the Jedi [[Ahsoka Tano]] and [[Kit Fisto]]. Despite resistance from the fugitives and the arrival of [[Gungan]] reinforcements, the Quarren and Tamson's [[Confederacy military|Separatist forces]] succeeded in capturing the fugitives.<ref name="Gungan Attack">{{TCW|Gungan Attack}}</ref> However, the Quarren-Separatist alliance fell apart after Nossor Ri learned that Tamson intended to crown himself as the new ruler of Mon Cala. Ri foiled Tamson's plot to execute Prince Lee-Char, who wanted to restore relations between the Mon Calamari and Quarren. The Quarren then joined forces with the Mon Calamari, the Republic, the Jedi, and the Gungans in a combined effort to expel the Separatist invaders from Mon Cala. Following the death of Tamson, the Quarren accepted Lee-Char as the new [[King of Mon Cala]].<ref name="Prisoners" />

===Imperial and First Order eras===
{{Quote|<nowiki></nowiki>''For Mon Cala! We will fight until our dying''&mdash;|The last words of Nossor Ri|<ref name="Allegiance 4">[[Allegiance 4|''Allegiance'' 4]]</ref>}}
After uncovering the sinister Separatist plot and re-aligning themselves with the Mon Calamari, the Quarren and Mon Calamari fought as allies to uphold peace, from the final stages of the Clone Wars and throughout the [[Galactic Civil War]].<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref> Early in the [[Imperial Era]], Quarren and Mon Calamari fought alongside each other against the Empire's [[invasion of Mon Cala]].<ref name="Dark Lord 14">[[Darth Vader (2017) 14|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 14]]</ref> The Quarren [[Chadkol Gee]] lost his [[Chadkol Gee's family|family]] to the Empire during the [[occupation of Mon Cala]].<ref name="Allegiance 2">[[Allegiance 2|''Allegiance'' 2]]</ref> Later, by joining together, the two species were able to wipe out the occupying Imperial garrison.<ref name="BMF 24">{{BuildFalconCite|24|Starship Fact File}}</ref> During the [[New Republic Era]], the Quarren and Mon Calamari finally had their long awaited peace.<ref name="Chapter 22">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 22: Guns for Hire}}</ref>

Following the [[Battle of Crait]], [[Resistance]] agents [[Mission to Mon Cala|travelled to Mon Cala]] for help in the battle against the [[First Order]], earning the ire of the now-General Nossor Ri, who did not want more destruction brought upon the peoples of Mon Cala.<ref name="Allegiance 1">[[Allegiance 1|''Allegiance'' 1]]</ref> Chadkol Gee, however, contacted the First Order about the Resistance mission, resulting in a First Order fleet appearing over Mon Cala. After Gee's crime was revealed and King [[Ech-Char]] decided to give the Resistance the reinforcements they sought, Ri chose to sacrifice himself to allow the Resistance a chance to escape and to make up for what Gee had done. After Ri was killed and the Resistance escaped, First Order forces landed on Mon Cala to enact revenge upon the Quarren and Mon Calamari for daring to help the Resistance, further convincing Gee that he had been right all along.<ref name="Allegiance 4" />

==Quarren in the galaxy==
[[File:Quarren_-_SW_Battlefront.png|thumb|left|175px|A Quarren Rebel trooper.]]
Several Quarren individuals could be found throughout [[the galaxy]] in various walks of life. [[Christo]],<ref name="Pursuit of Peace" /> Tikkes,<ref name="Episode II" /> and Tundra Dowmeia<ref name="USW" /> served as senators in the Galactic Senate during the last [[Standard day|days]] of the Galactic Republic. These senators used bathing pools to keep their skin moist.<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> Orlen Mollo was a jovial Quarren who served as a Supreme Chancellor of the Republic, holding the [[Office of the Chancellor]] jointly with the human [[Kyong Greylark]]. With Greylark remaining on Coruscant, Mollo was free to travel the Outer Rim aboard the [[Alif-class Longbeam|''Alif''-class Longbeam]] ''[[Paxion]]'' to help his citizens. Meeting Jedi Knight [[Gella Nattai]] after an impressive [[pilot]]ing display during the [[skirmish in the Eiram system]], Mollo slapped her on the back in greeting, which she took as odd behavior for a Chancellor and a Quarren.<ref name="Convergence" />

[[File:KraganGorrPirateCaptain-CM.png|thumb|275px|Kragan Gorr]]
One Quarren migrant named [[Lauli Wahlo]] operated a [[Galaxy Noodles|noodle shop]] in [[Coruscant]]'s [[Coruscant Underworld|underworld]]<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" /> while another Quarren migrant named [[Amit Noloff]] was a member of the [[Iego council]].<ref name="Mystery of a Thousand Moons" /> During the Galactic Civil War, [[Tessek]] worked as a book-keeper for [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]] on the planet [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> During the Clone Wars, many Quarren were employed by Jabba Desilijic Tiure to serve him as guards.<ref name="Eminence">{{TCW|Eminence (episode)}}</ref> The former slave Quarren [[Palabar]], along with his companions the [[Wookiee]] [[Greybok]] and the [[Weequay]] [[Hatchet]], took part in the [[New Republic]]'s [[Liberation of Kashyyyk|liberation]] of [[Kashyyyk]].<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref> The Quarren [[Kragan Gorr]] was part of [[Grox]]'s [[Grox's pirate crew|pirate crew]] in his early life<ref name="Luke & Leia">''[[Choose Your Destiny: A Luke & Leia Adventure]]''</ref> and later led his own [[pirate]] group, the [[Warbird gang]].<ref name="Triple Dark">{{Resistance|The Triple Dark}}</ref>

[[Kara Xoo]] was a Quarren [[Nihil]] [[Tempest Runner]] during the High Republic Era.<ref name="OotS">''[[The High Republic: Out of the Shadows]]''</ref> Another [[Unidentified Quarren (Lula Talisola)|Quarren]] was present on the planet [[Eiram]] in the wake of the [[Destruction of Starlight Beacon]] and crossed paths with the amnestic [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Lula Mrala-Talisola|Lula Talisola]].<ref name="THRA 2">[[The High Republic Adventures (2023) 2|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2023) 2]]</ref>  Quarren Heavy Gunners were Quarren soldiers in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="Battlefront I">''[[Star Wars Battlefront]]''</ref> A Quarren nicknamed "[[Squawk (Quarren)|Squawk]]" was a [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[agent]] who worked with the [[Jedi]] [[Sean]] and [[Mostima]] during the High Republic Era.<ref name="Vow">''[[The Vow of Silver Dawn]]''</ref> The Quarren [[Hennix]] was a [[Padawan]] in [[Luke Skywalker]]'s [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Rise of Kylo Ren">[[The Rise of Kylo Ren 1|''The Rise of Kylo Ren'' 1]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Quarren first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']],"<ref name="Episode VI" /> which was first released on [[May 25]], [[1983]].

